    <bpmn:startEvent id="startE_6e66bf31" name="Issue requires community input">
      <bpmn:documentation>Page: Wikipedia:Requests for comment/2014/November  Question: Should cross-wiki filters exist at all?  Options: Yes, No  RFC ID: 2A1B3C4  Opened: 2014-11-05</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_20f419a9</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:userTask id="userTa_15a79ffb" name="Open RFC: Glaisher">
      <bpmn:documentation>Should cross-wiki filters exist at all?</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_20f419a9</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_67880c54</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:task id="task_165ed40b" name="Listed by Legobot — categories: policy">
      <bpmn:documentation>Auto-listed in central RFC tables for advertised participation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_67880c54</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_222d4999</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:userTask id="userTa_5c0dd9e7" name="Community discussion (3S / 1O / 1N / 1Alt)">
      <bpmn:documentation>Support voters: Glaisher, Stryn, Jasper Deng  Oppose voters: Ningauble  Top arguments for: Helps with dealing with cross-wiki abuse (spam in particular) and makes local admins' jobs easier. | Local admins should have the rights to view global filters. | Formalizing the process for global abuse filter editor, including a week of discussion before granting the right.  Top arguments against: Concerned about the use of these filters for outright censorship.  Involved/uninvolved breakdown: 6 involved / 1 uninvolved</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_222d4999</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_41c4f301</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:task id="task_9efcf812" name="30-day discussion period (Legobot delists)">
      <bpmn:documentation>Default RFC duration; can be extended for ongoing discussion</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_41c4f301</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_62217a93</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:userTask id="userTa_c47e20b2" name="Closer summary: PiRSquared17 (admin)">
      <bpmn:documentation>Closed: 2014-11-01  Summary: The discussion concluded with broad support for granting local administrators the ability to view global abuse filters and the abuse logs, as well as formalizing a process for requesting abuse filter editor rights. Stewards' editing rights were affirmed.  Next: no action</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_62217a93</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_98d34b38</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="exclus_106124d5" name="Consensus finding?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Branch codes:  SS = strong consensus support  •  RS = rough consensus support  •  NC = no consensus  •  RO = rough consensus oppose  •  SO = strong consensus oppose  •  W = withdrawn  •  SC = speedy close  •  U = unknown</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_98d34b38</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_7041cc0e</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_019d3069</bpmn:outgoing>
